### **4. Identified Risks for Each Risk Class**

#### **Risk 1:**
**Description:**
The **dog crossing the road** poses a **high collision risk** for the **ego vehicle (red pickup truck)** and **nearby vehicles (red sports car, green SUV)**. The dog’s unpredictable movement and proximity to moving vehicles increase the likelihood of an accident.

**Severity Score:** **0.95** (Very High)

#### **Risk 2:**
**Description:**
The **ego vehicle (red pickup truck)** is **following too closely** behind the **green SUV**, reducing reaction time if the SUV brakes suddenly. This increases the risk of a **rear-end collision**.

**Severity Score:** **0.75** (High)

#### **Risk 3:**
**Description:**
The **dog’s crossing path** is **unpredictable**, and its **sudden movements** may cause **distraction or panic** in nearby drivers, leading to **loss of control** or **swerving**.

**Severity Score:** **0.85** (High)

#### **Risk 4:**
**Description:**
The **red sports car** is **too close to the dog**, increasing the risk of **collision if the dog changes direction abruptly**.

**Severity Score:** **0.80** (High)

#### **Risk 5:**
**Description:**
The **ego vehicle’s camera perspective** (from the hood) may **occlude parts of the road**, reducing visibility of **small objects (e.g., the dog)** until they are very close.

**Severity Score:** **0.60** (Moderate)

